Description: web documents as first-class files for the Linux desktop
 webdoc makes a .web file an ordinary filesystem object representing a web
 URL together with a little metadata: an optional browser selection and an
 optional lock.
 .
 A .web file owns all of its own persistent state, so documents can be
 created anywhere, renamed, moved, copied, version-controlled and deleted
 with ordinary tools. There is no database, no index and no daemon.
 .
 This package provides the web command line tool, its manual page and the
 desktop MIME integration that lets a file manager open a .web file in a
 browser.

